[17592186302906 1145 "To solve this problem, we use the formula\n\n$$\ns=ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the displacement, measured from the starting position in the direction of the initial motion, $u$ is the initial velocity, $t$ is the time since the beginning of the motion, and $g$ is the acceleration due to gravity.\n\nLet's summarize the information we have:\n\n- The coin falls for $t=12\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n- The coin covers the distance of $s=720\\,\\text{m}.$\n\n- The acceleration due to gravity is $g=9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula and solving for $u,$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2} \\\\ (720) & =u(12)+\\frac{1}{2}(9.8)(12)^{2} \\\\ 720 & =12u+705.6 \\\\ 14.4 & =12u \\\\ u & =1.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the initial velocity of the coin was $1.2\\,\\text{m/s}.$" 13194139534678 true] [17592186302907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302908 13194139534678 true] [17592186302907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302909 13194139534678 true] [17592186302907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302910 13194139534678 true] [17592186302907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302911 13194139534678 true] [17592186302907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302912 13194139534678 true] [17592186302907 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534678 true] [17592186302907 1041 "selection" 13194139534678 true] [17592186302907 1104 #edb/ref 17592186302912 13194139534678 true] [17592186302907 1110 #uuid "c670b444-9c5a-5118-9955-566fc9f3647a" 13194139534678 true] [17592186302908 1034 "5.1\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139534678 true] [17592186302908 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534678 true] [17592186302908 1111 #uuid "15fc59e3-0dbf-53f1-8e46-c0d37301684c" 13194139534678 true] [17592186302909 1034 "7.6\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139534678 true] [17592186302909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534678 true] [17592186302909 1111 #uuid "1e49e830-c63f-5747-8b14-bc97b2987f1d" 13194139534678 true] [17592186302910 1034 "3.2\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139534678 true]